&Q000451 = A praise poem of Išme-Dagan (Išme-Dagan A + V)
@composite
#project: etcslatf/inter
#atf: use unicode
#atf: use math
#etcsl: text-id=c.2.5.4.01
#key: after http://etcsl.orinst.ox.ac.uk/cgi-bin/etcsl.cgi?text=c.2.5.4.01&display=Crit&charenc=gcirc#

@div segment A

A.1. {[d]}[en-lil₂ dirig-še₃ ...]
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; dirig[make more than]; X
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, by far ……  
#etcsl: line-id=A.1

#etcsl#cite Cited in OB catalogue in the Louvre, 0.2.02, line 58; OB catalogue from Urim (U2), 0.2.04, line 51

A.2. [...]
#lem: X
#tr.en: He to whom the great gods pay attention; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.2

A.3. X [...]
#lem: X; X
#tr.en: foundation deposit of the @wDN{Anuna}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.3

A.4. diŋir gal-gal-e-ne saŋ keše₂#-[bi]
#lem: diŋir[deity]; gal[big]; saŋ[head]; kešed[bind]
#tr.en: living …… of the @wDN{Enki} deities; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.4

A.5. {d}a-nun-na-ke₄-ne temen-bi
#lem: Anunak[1]DN; temen[foundation]
#tr.en: he whose great divine powers know no opponents, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.5

A.6. {d}en-ki-{d}en-ki tug₂ zi-ŋal₂-bi
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; tug[textile]; ziŋal[living things]
#tr.en: whose …… excel all others, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.6

A.7. me gal-gal-a-ni sag₂ di nu-zu
#lem: me[Being]; gal[big]; sag[scatter]; di[speak]; zu[know]
#tr.en: whose …… is achieved by no one; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.7

A.8. [...]-ni# saŋ-bi-še₃ e₃-a
#lem: X; saŋ[head]; e[leave]
#tr.en: whose …… return of their own accord, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.8

A.9. [...]-ni# na-me sa₂ nu-di
#lem: X; name[any]; sa[equal]; di[speak]
#tr.en: whose …… is very sweet in heaven and on earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.9

A.10. [...]-me-ni ni₂-ba gi₄-gi₄
#lem: X; ni[self]; gi[turn]
#tr.en: whose …… founds cities, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.10

A.11. [...]-ni an ki-bi dug₃-dug₃
#lem: X; an[sky]; ki[place]; dug[good]
#tr.en: whose …… establishes the Land; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.11

A.12. [...]-ni iri ki du₃-du₃
#lem: X; iri[city]; ki[place]; du[build]
#tr.en: …… wisdom is perfect as time passes; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.12

A.13. [...]-ni kalam ki ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#lem: X; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: …… wise in command, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.13

A.14. [...] X ŋeštug₂ ud zal-la šu du₇
#lem: X; X; ŋeštug[ear]; ud[sun]; zal[pass time]; šu[hand]; du[perfect]
#tr.en: re-establishing justice ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.14

A.15. [...] a₂ aŋ₂-e gal-zu
#lem: X; a[arm]; aŋ[measure]; galanzu[wise]
#tr.en: adviser who never tires of discussion; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.15

A.16. [...] A niŋ₂-zid ki-bi-še₃ ŋar
#lem: X; X; niŋzid[righteousness]; ki[place]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: ……, giving verdicts, ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.16

A.17. [ad gi₄]-gi₄# inim-ma nu-kuš₂-u₃
#lem: ad[voice]; gi[turn]; inim[word]; kušu[tired]
#tr.en: judge of heaven and earth  
#etcsl: line-id=A.17

A.18. A [...] eš-bar-e di-di
#lem: X; X; ešbar[decision]; did[lawsuit]
#tr.en: guiding the living ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.18

A.19. X [...]-ma di-kud an ki
#lem: X; X; dikud[judge]; an[sky]; ki[place]
#tr.en: Father @wDN{Enlil}, shepherd of the black-headed, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.19

A.20. X [...]-ni-še₃ ŋal₂-la
#lem: X; X; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: by his …… making the foreign countries bow low. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.20

A.21. niŋ₂-[zi]-ŋal₂# X X lah₅#-lah₅-e
#lem: niŋziŋal[living creature]; X; X; lah[plural stem of tum ⟦bring⟧]
#etcsl: line-id=A.21

A.22. a-[a] {[d]}en-lil₂ sipad saŋ gig₂-ga
#lem: aya[father]; Enlil[1]DN; sipad[shepherd]; saŋ[head]; giggig[black]
#etcsl: line-id=A.22

A.23. X [...] X-ni-ta kur gam-e
#lem: X; X; X; kur[mountain(s)]; gurum[bend]
#etcsl: line-id=A.23

A.24. [...]-ni# zag an ki gen₆-ne₂
#lem: X; zag[side]; an[sky]; ki[place]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: He whose …… strengthens the boundaries of heaven and earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.24

A.25. [inim] dug₄-ga-ni ka teš₂-e ŋa₂-ŋa₂
#lem: inim[word]; dug[speak]; kag[mouth]; teš[unity]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: whose utterances unite them; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.25

A.26. en# li-ib-a-ni kur-ra du-du
#lem: en[lord]; lib[daze]; kur[mountain(s)]; ŋen[go]
#tr.en: lord whose ominous silence pervades the foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.26

A.27. niŋ₂# ak-ni su zig₃ ri-a
#lem: niŋ[thing]; ak[do]; su[flesh]; zig[rise]; ri[impose]
#tr.en: whose actions are spine-chilling, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.27

A.28. di galam-ma-ni na-me nu-pad₃-de₃
#lem: did[lawsuit]; galam[skilful]; name[any]; pad[find]
#tr.en: whose complex judgments cannot be revealed by anyone, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.28

A.29. nam-zu-ni-še₃ kur-re giri₁₇ šu ŋal₂
#lem: namzu[wisdom]; kur[mountain(s)]; kiri[nose]; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: whose knowledge is honoured by the foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.29

A.30. a₂ sa-par₄ gal kur-re dub-ba
#lem: a[arm]; sabar[net]; gal[big]; kur[mountain(s)]; dub[heap up]
#tr.en: whose strength is a great battle-net …… the foreign lands, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.30

A.31. sa-al-hub₂ IGI ŠU GAN nu-še-ga šu₂-a
#lem: salhub[net]; X; X; X; šeg[agree]; šuš[cover]
#tr.en: a fine-mesh battle-net …… covering the disobedient; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.31

A.32. an-še₃ DU ki-tuš ŋa₂-la nu-dag-ge
#lem: an[sky]; X; kituš[dwelling place]; ŋala[cvne]; dag[roam around]
#tr.en: indefatigable …… in heaven, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.32

A.33. me niŋ₂-nam-ma da-ga-an-ba šu ti-a
#lem: me[Being]; niŋnam[anything]; dagan[totality]; šu[hand]; teŋ[approach]
#tr.en: in possession of every one of the divine powers in their totality, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.33

A.34. ŋiš-hur niŋ₂-ul-e zag keše₂-ra₂
#lem: ŋešhur[plan]; niŋul[an everlasting thing]; zag[side]; kešed[bind]
#tr.en: linking together the ancient plans; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.34

A.35. ub-da 4-ba u₁₈-lu i₃-dul₄
#lem: ub[corner]; n; ulu[south wind]; dul[cover]
#tr.en: south wind which covers the four quarters; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.35

A.36. {d}en-lil₂ dib-ba-ni šu tiŋ₄-ŋe₂₆-e nu-zu
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; dib[pass]; šu[hand]; teŋ[approach]; zu[know]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.36

A.37. a-ar₂-ni niŋ₂ šu sag₃-sag₃-ge₂-dam
#lem: ar[celebrate]; niŋ[thing]; šu[hand]; sag[strike]
#tr.en: whose …… cannot be grasped, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.37

A.38. {d}en-lil₂ an-še₃ mah ki-še₃ dib
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; an[sky]; mah[great]; ki[place]; dib[pass]
#tr.en: whose fame is enough to make people quake; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.38

A.39. zag e₃ ki-en-gi-ra daŋal tag-ga
#lem: zag[side]; e[leave]; Kengir[1]; daŋal[wide]; tag[touch]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, great in heaven, surpassing on earth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.39

A.40. {d}nu-nam-nir en nun-nun-e-ne lugal-a lugal-be₂-e
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; en[lord]; nun[prince]; lugal[king]; lugal[king]
#tr.en: exceptional and wide-reaching in @wGN{Sumer}, @wDN{Nunamnir}, lord of princes, king of kings! 
#etcsl: line-id=A.40

A.41. {d}iš-me-{d}da-gan dumu {d}da-gan-na-me-en
#lem: Išmedagan[1]RN; dumu[child]; Dagan[1]DN
#tr.en: He determined a good destiny in the holy city for me, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.41

A.42. iri# kug-ga nam dug₃ ha-ma-ni-in-tar
#lem: iri[city]; kug[pure]; nam[fate]; dug[good]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: @wRN{Išme-@wDN{Dagan}}, son of @wDN{Dagan}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.42

A.43. a šag₄-ga ru-a-ŋa₂ mu dug₃ ha-ma-ni-in-sa₄
#lem: a[water]; šag[heart]; ri[impose]; mu[name]; dug[good]; še[call by name]
#tr.en: He named me with a favourable name even when my seed was inserted into the womb. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.43

A.44. {[d]}nin-tur₅ tud-tud-a ha-ma-ni-in-gub
#lem: Nintur[1]DN; utud[give birth (to)]; gub[stand]
#tr.en: @wDN{Nintur} stood by at my birth, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.44

A.45. gi#-dur ku₅-ra₂-ŋa₂ [...] nam-en ha-ma-ni-in-ŋar
#lem: dur[umbilical cord]; kud[cut]; X; namen[the office of en-priest]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: and she established the office of @fsux{en} for me ……, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.45

A.46. {[d]}en-lil₂ diŋir saŋ-du-ŋa₂-ke₄
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; diŋir[deity]; saŋdu[head]
#tr.en: even when my umbilical cord was cut. @wDN{Enlil}, my principal deity, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.46

A.47. nam-sipad ki-en-gi-ra saŋ-e-eš hu-mu-rig₇
#lem: namsipad[shepherdship]; Kengir[1]; saŋ[head]; rig[donate]
#tr.en: bestowed on me the shepherdship of @wGN{Sumer}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.47

A.48. {d}lamma ŋa₂-la nu-dag-ge saŋ# he₂-mi-in-tuku
#lem: lammar[(female) tutelary deity]; ŋala[cvne]; dag[roam around]; saŋ[head]; tuku[acquire]
#tr.en: and assigned to me a tireless protective goddess, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.48

A.49. alan niŋ₂-gen₆-na he₂-en-ga-da#-tah
#lem: alan[image]; niŋgina[truth]; tah[add]
#tr.en: adding also therewith a correct stature. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.49

A.50. [...] KA bal-en
#lem: X; X; bala[turn]
#etcsl: line-id=A.50

A.51. X [...] ha-ma-ni-in-kur₉
#lem: X; X; kur[enter]
#etcsl: line-id=A.51

A.52. su X [...] X hu-mu-UD-MU
#lem: su[flesh]; X; X; X; X
#etcsl: line-id=A.52

A.53. me-lem₄-[a-ni kur]-ra he₂-bi₂-in-X
#lem: melim[frightening splendor]; kur[mountain(s)]; X
#tr.en: His splendour …… the mountains, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.53

A.54. za-pa-aŋ₂-[a-ni] an ki-a he₂-em-mi-in-dirig
#lem: zipaŋ[voice]; an[sky]; ki[place]; dirig[make more than]
#tr.en: and his roar reaches beyond heaven and earth. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.54

A.55. uŋ₃-ŋa₂ hu#-[mu]-ni-in-suh-en kalam he₂-ni-in-pad₃-[en]
#lem: uŋ[people]; suh[choose]; kalam[the Land (of Sumer)]; pad[find]
#tr.en: He selected me from my people, and announced me to the Land. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.55

A.56. {d}en-lil₂ lugal diŋir-re-e-ne-ke₄
#lem: Enlil[1]DN; lugal[king]; diŋir[deity]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil}, king of the gods, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.56

A.57. sig igi-nim-ma nam-en-bi ha-ma-an-šum₂
#lem: sig[weak]; iginim[upper land]; namen[the office of en-priest]; šum[give]
#tr.en: gave me lordship over the south and over the uplands. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.57

A.58. inim dug₄-ga {d}nu-nam-nir-ra-ta
#lem: inim[word]; dug[speak]; Nunamnir[1]DN
#tr.en: At @wDN{Nunamnir's} instigation, @wDN{An} spoke encouragingly to me, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.58

A.59. an-ne₂ gu₃ zid-de₃ ŋa₂-a-ar ha-ma-an-de₂
#lem: An[1]DN; gu[voice]; zid[right]; ŋaʾe[I]; de[pour]
#tr.en: and placed crook and staff in my hands. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.59

A.60. šibir ešgiri₂ šu-ŋu₁₀ ha-ma-šum₂
#lem: šibir[shepherd's staff]; ešgiri[staff]; šu[hand]; šum[give]
#tr.en: @wDN{Uraš} nursed me on her holy knees. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.60

A.61. {d}uraš-e dub₃ kug-ga-ni-a mi₂ zid ha-ma-ni-dug₄
#lem: Uraš[1]DN; dub[knee]; kug[pure]; mi[cvne]; zid[right]; dug[speak]
#tr.en: In the @wTN{Ki-ur}, the great place, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.61

A.62. {d}nin-lil₂-le šag₄ zalag-zalag-ga-ni
#lem: Ninlil[1]DN; šag[heart]; zalag[bright]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninlil} in her radiant heart determined as my destiny that I should sit on an exalted dais until distant days, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.62

A.63. barag mah ud su₃-ra₂-ka tuš-ŋa₂
#lem: barag[sanctum]; mah[great]; ud[sun]; sud[distant]; tuš[sit (down)]
#tr.en: to enjoy in favour the reign which is my lot; 
#etcsl: line-id=A.63

A.64. ŋiš-šub-ba-ŋa₂ bal-bi sag₉-ge-da
#lem: ŋeššub[lot]; bala[turn]; sag[good]
#tr.en: that I should delight @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.64

A.65. su {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ka dug₃-ge-ŋa₂
#lem: su[flesh]; Enlil[1]DN; dug[good]
#tr.en: and that I should daily attend to the @wTN{E-kur}. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.65

A.66. e₂-kur-re ud šu₂-uš saŋ us₂-ŋa₂
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; ud[sun]; šuš[cover]; saŋ[head]; us[accompany]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enki}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.66

A.67. ki-ur₃ ki gal-e nam-še₃ ha-ma-ni-tar
#lem: Kiʾur[1]; ki[place]; gal[big]; nam[fate]; tar[cut]
#tr.en: the great lord of @wSN{Eridug}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.67

A.68. {d}en-ki en gal eridug{ki}-ga-ke₄
#lem: Enkik[1]DN; en[lord]; gal[big]; Eridug[1]SN
#tr.en: confirmed for me the good and great crown, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.68

A.69. aga₃ zid mah saŋ-ŋa₂ ha-ma-ni-in-ge-en
#lem: aga[tiara]; zid[right]; mah[great]; saŋ[head]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: …… everything, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.69

A.70. niŋ₂ a-na mu sa₄-a X X [...]
#lem: niŋ[thing]; ana[what?]; mu[name]; še[call by name]; X; X; X
#tr.en: and richly conferred on me seven wisdoms. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.70

A.71. ŋeštug₂ 7-a šu gal ha-ma#-[ni-du₇]
#lem: ŋeštug[ear]; n; šu[hand]; gal[big]; du[perfect]
#tr.en: @wDN{Suen}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.71

A.72. {d}suen dumu-saŋ {d}en-lil₂#-[la₂-ke₄]
#lem: Suen[1]DN; dumusaŋ[first-born]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: the firstborn son of @wDN{Enlil}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.72

A.73. {ŋiš}gu-za lugal-la me ur₄#-[ur₄ ...]
#lem: guza[chair]; lugal[king]; me[Being]; ur[gather]; X
#tr.en: …… for me a royal throne that gathers together the divine powers, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.73

A.74. barag nam-en-na saŋ-bi-še₃ [e₃]-a he₂-bi₂#-in-[ŋar]
#lem: barag[sanctum]; namen[the office of en-priest]; saŋ[head]; e[leave]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: established an excellent lordly dais, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.74

A.75. ud su₃-ra₂-še₃ aga-ŋu₁₀# dalla# he₂-bi₂-in-e₃
#lem: ud[sun]; sud[distant]; aga[tiara]; dalla[(to be) bright]; e[leave]
#tr.en: and made my crown shine brilliantly until distant days. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.75

A.76. {d}nuska sukkal {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: Nuska[1]DN; sukkal[secretary]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: @wDN{Nuska}, @wDN{Enlil's} minister, placed the royal sceptre in my hand, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.76

A.77. ŋidru nam-lugal-la šu-ŋa₂ ha-ma-ni-ŋar
#lem: ŋidru[scepter]; namlugal[kingship]; šu[hand]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: revealed the powers of @wTN{E-kur} to me, established there for me an awe-inspiring podium, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.77

A.78. e₂-kur-ra a₂-bi ha-ma-an-pad₃-pad₃
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; a[arm]; pad[find]
#tr.en: and ensured that @wDN{Enlil's} heart was in a joyful mood. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.78

A.79. ki-gub-bu ni₂ teŋ₃-ŋe₂₆-e-bi ha-ma-an-ŋar
#lem: kigub[station]; ni[fear]; teŋ[approach]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: @wDN{Ninurta}, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.79

A.80. šag₄ {d}en-lil₂-la₂ hul₂-la-am₃-ta he₂-mi-ge-en₆
#lem: šag[heart]; Enlil[1]DN; hul[rejoice]; gin[confirm]
#tr.en: @wDN{Enlil's} mighty warrior, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.80

A.81. {d}nin-urta ur-saŋ kalag-ga {d}en-lil₂-la₂-ke₄
#lem: Ninurtak[1]DN; ursaŋ[warrior]; kalag[strong]; Enlil[1]DN
#tr.en: approached @wDN{Nunamnir} in speech on my behalf and secured (?) the favourable words of @wDN{Enlil} and @wDN{Ninlil} for me. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.81

A.82. {d}nu-nam-nir inim-ma ha-ma-ni-in-DU
#lem: Nunamnir[1]DN; inim[word]; X
#tr.en: He has made my reign of kingship excellent, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.82

A.83. inim sag₉-ga {d}en-lil₂ {d}nin-lil₂-la₂ ŋa₂-a-ar hu-mu-na-aŋ₂
#lem: inim[word]; sag[good]; Enlil[1]DN; Ninlil[1]DN; ŋaʾe[I]; aŋ[measure]
#tr.en: has made me great in lordship, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.83

A.84. nam-lugal-la bal-ŋu₁₀ he₂-bi₂-in-dirig
#lem: namlugal[kingship]; bala[turn]; dirig[make more than]
#tr.en: and is indeed my helper. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.84

A.85. nam-en-na ŋe₂₆-e he₂-em-mi-in-gal-e a₂-tah-ŋu₁₀ he₂-e
#lem: namen[the office of en-priest]; ŋaʾe[I]; gal[big]; atah[helper]; me[be]
#tr.en: In @wTN{E-kur} he prays continually on my behalf, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.85

A.86. e₂-kur-ra šu hu-mu-da-ŋal₂-ŋal₂
#lem: Ekur[1]TN; šu[hand]; ŋal[⟦be⟧ to be (there]
#tr.en: and is indeed the constable of my kingship. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.86

A.87. maškim nam-lugal-ŋa₂ he₂-e
#lem: maškim[an administrator]; namlugal[kingship]; me[be]
#tr.en: He, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.87

A.88. {ŋiš}tukul kalag-ga kur-kur gam-gam-e
#lem: tukul[weapon]; kalag[strong]; kur[mountain(s)]; gurum[bend]
#tr.en: who with mighty weapons makes all the foreign countries bow low, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.88

A.89. a₂ mah šu zid-da-ŋu₁₀ NI he₂-bi₂-in-si
#lem: a[arm]; mah[great]; šu[hand]; zid[right]; X; si[fill]
#tr.en: has put great power …… into my right hand. 
#etcsl: line-id=A.89

A.90. {d}utu niŋ₂-si-sa₂ inim gen₆-na ka-ŋa₂ ha-ma-ni-in-ŋar
#lem: Utu[1]DN; niŋsisa[justice]; inim[word]; gin[confirm]; kag[mouth]; ŋar[put]
#tr.en: @wDN{Utu} put justice and reliable words in my mouth. To make judgments, 
#etcsl: line-id=A.90

